<title>SINGAPORE: QAF LTD half year net down 22.5 pct.</title>
<headline>QAF LTD half year net down 22.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 6.23	vs     8.04</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)		1.97	vs     2.55</p>
<p>    Turnover			 151.13	vs   178.56</p>
<p>    Investment income		0.86	vs     nil</p>
<p>    Other income		     0.34	vs     0.34</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 1.37	vs     1.27</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		   9.06	vs    12.06</p>
<p>    Tax				  2.84	vs     3.09</p>
<p>    Minorities			 0.004     vs    (0.94)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		 (0.11)     vs     nil</p>
<p>Note- Bread manufacturer and distributor QAF Ltd said the extraordinary items were due to takeover expense for Qualif Pte Ltd and write-back of expenses on disposal of subsidiaries. It said pre-tax profit fell due to exclusion of contribution from its Brunei group and costs associated with start-up bakery operations in India and China.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
